  "reasoning": "Cook Political Report\u2019s statewide PVI list shows New Mexico at roughly D+4, indicating a modest but consistent Democratic structural advantage in federal elections.[1][5][3] Recent 2026-cycle coverage from major handicappers like Cook and Sabato\u2019s Crystal Ball rates the open New Mexico gubernatorial race as Solid/Safe Democratic, and local reporting notes Democratic federal incumbents (Sen. Ben Ray Luj\u00e1n and Reps. Stansbury, Vasquez, and Leger Fern\u00e1ndez) all holding sizable fundraising leads over their Republican challengers, reinforcing a clear Democratic edge.[7][9][10] While I could not locate head\u2011to\u2011head federal polling within the last 45 days, the combination of a D+4 PVI baseline and current-cycle indicators (safe/Solid D governor ratings and multi\u2011million\u2011dollar Democratic cash advantages versus GOP opponents) supports a present lean Democratic environment by an estimated mid\u2011single\u2011digit margin rather than a true toss\u2011up.[1][7][9][10]",
